NAME
       buildah - build container images

SYNOPSIS
       buildah build [-t NAME[:TAG]] [-f FILE] [DIRECTORY]
       buildah images

DESCRIPTION
       buildah builds OCI container images. It shares its image store with
       podman (for root in /var/lib/containers, for a normal user in
       ~/.local/share/containers), so an image built with buildah is
       listed by podman images and the other way round.

       buildah build (also called buildah bud, "build using dockerfile")
       reads a Containerfile (or Dockerfile) in DIRECTORY and runs its steps,
       just like podman build, which uses the same code.

       It comes with the container-tools package.

OPTIONS
       -t NAME[:TAG], --tag NAME[:TAG]
              Name the new image.

       -f FILE, --file FILE
              Use FILE instead of DIRECTORY/Containerfile.

EXAMPLES
       Build an image from the Containerfile in the current directory:

           buildah build -t myweb:1.0 .

       List the images:

           buildah images

NOTES
       Cert Lab includes buildah build and buildah images; for everything else
       use podman.

SEE ALSO
       podman(1), podman-build(1), skopeo(1)
